From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000084 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: copy init stack through uncached alias

The uncached-init-stack hardware log gets as far as the copied /init stack
path, then traps with Reserved Instruction at __kmap_pgprot's tlbwi. The GUP
path pinned the page, but kmap(page) tried to install a temporary TLB mapping
on a CPU where Linux TLB writes are not yet viable.

Copy the pinned stack page through its KSEG1 physical alias instead. That keeps
the page pinning and existing stack remap diagnostics, but avoids another TLB
writer before the first userspace instruction can run.
---
 fs/binfmt_elf.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/fs/binfmt_elf.c
+++ b/fs/binfmt_elf.c
@@ -423,6 +423,7 @@ static int sf2000_elf_copy_identity_stack(unsigned long *sp)
 	long pinned;
 	void *src;
 	void *dst;
+	unsigned long src_phys;
 	unsigned long mapped;
 	unsigned long src_addr = *sp & PAGE_MASK;
 	unsigned long low_sp = SF2000_IDENTITY_STACK_PAGE +
@@ -442,12 +443,14 @@ static int sf2000_elf_copy_identity_stack(unsigned long *sp)
 		return -EFAULT;
 	}
 
-	src = kmap(page);
+	src_phys = (unsigned long)page_to_phys(page);
+	sf2000_elf_value("elf-id-stack-phys", (unsigned int)src_phys);
+	src = (void *)CKSEG1ADDR(src_phys);
+	sf2000_elf_value("elf-id-stack-copy-src", (unsigned int)src);
 	dst = (void *)CKSEG1ADDR(SF2000_IDENTITY_STACK_BASE);
 	memset(dst, 0, SF2000_IDENTITY_STACK_SIZE);
 	dst = (void *)CKSEG1ADDR(SF2000_IDENTITY_STACK_PAGE);
 	memcpy(dst, src, PAGE_SIZE);
-	kunmap(page);
 	put_page(page);
 	flush_cache_all();
 	mapped = vm_mmap(NULL, SF2000_IDENTITY_STACK_BASE,
